WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.687
Now the rest of the map.

2
00:00:01.687 --> 00:00:05.398
An application that calls
Microsoft Graph as a user account,

3
00:00:05.398 --> 00:00:09.686
moved to an app registration, gains
an app-registration certificate,

4
00:00:09.686 --> 00:00:13.899
at most a hundred and eighty days,
renewed by its owner or by Key Vault.

5
00:00:13.899 --> 00:00:18.159
The same application on Azure or on
an Arc-enabled server moves to a

6
00:00:18.159 --> 00:00:22.650
managed identity instead: none before,
none after, and Azure handles it.

7
00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:27.731
A workload outside AWS that uses an I A M
user's secret key can move to I A M Roles

8
00:00:27.731 --> 00:00:31.360
Anywhere, which needs an X
dot five-oh-nine certificate

9
00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:34.425
from the program's public
key infrastructure.

10
00:00:34.425 --> 00:00:36.403
The certificate platform issues it,

11
00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:39.700
and GovCloud needs certificate
revocation lists imported.

12
00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:42.883
And a R H E L host's
Active Directory keytab,

13
00:00:42.883 --> 00:00:48.032
moved to the platform's workload
identity, needs no certificate at

14
00:00:48.032 --> 00:00:52.525
all for an I A M role or an O C I
principal; AWS or O C I handles it.

15
00:00:52.525 --> 00:00:55.137
So certificates change shape, not count.

16
00:00:55.137 --> 00:00:59.191
A managed identity, an I A M role
and an O C I principal need none;

17
00:00:59.191 --> 00:01:03.500
an app registration and Roles
Anywhere each need a certificate.
